setEnv [SimTalk]
Sets the specified environment variable.
Remarks
If you deactivate the safety setting File > Model Settings > General > Prohibit Access to the Computer,
Plant Simulation does not run the function setEnv and shows an error message.
Type
Function
Syntax
setEnv(EnvironmentVariable:string, Value:string) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter EnvironmentVariable of data type string designates the name of the variable.
• The parameter Value of data type string designates its value.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Examples
setEnv("ralf","0")
startExtProc("PlantSimulation2606.exe")
In the external process you just started you can then query the value you set:
print getEnv("ralf") // returns the value of the variable
See also
Prohibit Access to the Computer [model settings]
getEnv [SimTalk]
setEnv [SimTalk]
